Z||000009||lowCG||06-06-2000||07:43 PM||||If there's bad rust anywhere else,I might try and find a replacement cradle.<BR>If the control arm is in good shape,then you could use it to locate the plate you weld in by bolting a plate to it,then tack welding to the subframe,remove the control arm,and finish the weld.Since it'd be difficult to weld inside the subframe,maybe a formed piece,plug-welded from the top and bottom would work better.||||reg||1
